  "variety": "it-IT",
  "subtitle": "Use e (and), o (or), ma (but) and perché (because, and also why) to join words and sentences. Before a word that starts with e-, e often becomes ed. Use anche for “also” and neanche or nemmeno for “not either”.",
  "briefMarks": ["e", "ed", "o", "ma", "perché", "anche", "neanche", "nemmeno"],
  "source": "icanspeak Italian original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-12)",
  "concept": {
